{"id":1,"title":"Descriptive Statistics","syllabus_module":"Module 1","question":"How do length, links, capitals and exclamation marks differ by class?","code":[{"label":"Training set only","file":"analysis/01_descriptive.R","start_line":12,"code":"emails <- arrow::read_parquet(\"data/processed/emails.parquet\")\ntrain <- as.data.frame(emails[emails$set == \"train\", ])\nfeatures <- c(\"body_chars\", \"n_urls\", \"caps_ratio\", \"exclam_count\")"},{"label":"Summary statistics for every feature x class","file":"analysis/01_descriptive.R","start_line":18,"code":"stats_tbl <- describe_by_class(train, features)"},{"label":"Choose log scale from skewness","file":"analysis/01_descriptive.R","start_line":21,"code":"# Log scale only for skewed features with a wide range (caps_ratio stays linear in [0, 1]).\nis_skewed <- vapply(features, function(f) {\n  min(stats_tbl$skewness[stats_tbl$feature == f]) > 1 && max(train[[f]]) > 10\n}, logical(1))"},{"label":"Descriptive summary of one variable","file":"R/rv.R","start_line":11,"code":"describe <- function(x) {\n  x <- x[!is.na(x)]\n  q <- stats::quantile(x, c(0.25, 0.5, 0.75), names = FALSE)\n  m <- mean(x)\n  s <- stats::sd(x)\n  c(\n    n = length(x), mean = m, median = q[2], mode = stat_mode(x),\n    q1 = q[1], q3 = q[3], iqr = q[3] - q[1], variance = s^2, sd = s,\n    cv = if (m != 0) s / m else NA_real_,\n    skewness = moments::skewness(x), kurtosis = moments::kurtosis(x)\n  )\n}"}],"console":["The tzdb package is not installed. Timezones will not be available to Arrow compute functions. If you get errors when using Arrow on datetimes, try running `install.packages('tzdb')` and trying again.","Train rows by class:","","legitimate   phishing       spam ","     27479       3388      26454 ","","Mean / median / SD by class:","      feature      class     mean   median       sd","   body_chars legitimate 2.14e+03 1.08e+03 4.89e+03","   body_chars   phishing 3.54e+03 2.09e+03 7.91e+04","   body_chars       spam 1.14e+03 3.93e+